<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Khurda</h1><p class="st-meta">1568 CE – 1804 CE (approx.) · capital Khurda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Odia kingdom that kept the Gajapati title and guarded the Jagannath temple at Puri under Mughal, Maratha and British overlords.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karrani-dynasty">Karrani Afghans</a> overthrew independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in 1568, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramachandra-deva-i">Ramachandra Deva I</a>, of the Bhoi family, established himself at Khurda near Puri. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar's</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-singh-i">Man Singh</a> recognised him as Raja of Khurda in 1592, and his successors took the Gajapati title of the former kings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Khurda rajas were acknowledged as the first servants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> at Puri, a role that gave them prestige across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. They ruled a small hill-and-forest territory with paika militia soldiers who held land for service. They paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> and, from 1751, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in 1803. The raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukunda-deva-ii">Mukunda Deva II</a> joined a revolt and Khurda was annexed in 1804. Resentment over land settlements led to the Paika Rebellion of 1817. The Puri Gajapati family still holds ritual rights at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> temple.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1568 CE – 1804 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.91%;width:4.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1568 CE – 1804 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khurda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ramachandra Deva I, Mukunda Deva II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism (Jagannath cult)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khurda, Bhoi kings of Khurda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=kingdom-of-khurda" aria-label="Kingdom of Khurda on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6834 1338 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Khurda lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1385h0M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7154 1594h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7154 1594h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=kingdom-of-khurda">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

